{{also|Schneiden}}
==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|snīden}}, from {{inh|de|goh|snīdan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*snīþan||to cut}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|nl|snijden||to cut, carve, intersect}}, {{cog|nds|snieden||to cut}}, dialectal {{cog|en|snithe||to cut}} (related to {{m|en|snide}}), {{cog|sv|snida||to carve, engrave}}, {{cog|is|sníða||to trim, tailor}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dn̩/|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-schneiden.ogg|Audio}}
* {{audio|de|De-schneiden2.ogg|Audio (Berlin)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|schneiden<schnitt,geschnitten>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[cut]]; to [[carve]]; to [[slice]]
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[pare]]; to [[clip]]; to [[mow]]; to [[prune]]; to [[trim]]
# {{lb|de|transitive|driving|figuratively}} to cut (someone) off; to cut in on (someone)
# {{lb|de|transitive|film}} to [[edit]]
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|reflexive}} to [[intersect]]
#: {{uxi|de|Die beiden Geraden '''schneiden''' sich.|Both streets intersect.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[cut]] (oneself)
# {{lb|de|reflexive|colloquial}} to [[delude]] (oneself); to become mistaken
# to [[avoid]] somebody (to cut someone)
<!-- Are there any intransitive senses? -->

